2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2366) 'A hook that needs the sound fails the viewer, and a short that is about us gives them nothing to do.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2366) 'Script the next short in the four beats before recording it, then count its frames against the length rule.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2366) 'a short runs forty seconds in four beats
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2366) 'A short runs exactly 40 seconds and is scripted before recording in four beats: hook, intrigue, delivery and exit (HIDE). The length is 40 times the frame rate in Movie Maker frames, counted from the first rendered frame. The engine renders the captions, and no external tool re-encodes the file.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2366) '- RFD66606-2294, where this rule lived before the split.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2366) 'The four beats
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2366) 'The hook fills the first 3 s as on-screen text that works with the sound off and promises without answering. One line of intrigue makes the viewer feel the problem. The delivery is the one thing they came for. The exit gives them something to do. It is never about us.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2366) 'Marketing media
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2366) 'Marketing media and samples are marked with `https://github.com/v-sekai-fire`: it is the `url` in each `.cff`, the web statement in its XMP and the line on its exit card, and each follows the four-beat script in this RFD.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2366  1 LINE
 Text:Written

